The open book is an open hardware e-book reader designed around the ESP32-S3, and a low-cost e-paper screen capable of displaying books in all the languages of the world Designed to be affordable, accessible, and DIY friendly, it aims to demystify the inner workings of consumer technology, and reclaim this essential technogical artifact as a piece of fully open-source hardware. 

